content:
Committee was minded to grant
planning permission for application reference
2025/2070/01/EIA:
 
 
(i) 
Subject to a section 106
agreement to secure:
 

­ 
Training employment plan contribution £10,000
and monitoring fee £2,500;

­ 
Maintenance of habitats and monitoring fee
£4,988;

­ 
SuDS Monitoring Contribution
£10,000;

­ 
Restrict occupation to student
accommodation;

­ 
Highways contributions for off-site
works;

­ 
Parks and recreation £195,930;

­ 
Open Space Contribution £51,024;

­ 
Securing demolition of walkways;

­ 
Private refuse collection for lifetime of
development;

­ 
Submission of a scheme for the public realm works
prior to commencement and requirement to deliver the scheme prior
to first occupation;

­ 
Associated monitoring costs arising from the above
planning obligations.
 
 (ii) 
Subject to the following conditions:
 
1. 
3 year consent;
2. 
List of approved drawings;
3. 
Samples of materials;
4. 
Paving details;
5. 
Large-scale details of the frieze (link
block);
6. 
Landscape structures to be developed as public
art;
7. 
Site Characterisation;
8. 
Submission of Remediation Scheme;
9. 
Implementation of Approved Remediation
Scheme;
10. 
Reporting of Unexpected Contamination;
11. 
Implemented in line with the drainage scheme
(Northumbrian Water);
12. 
The Biodiversity Gain Plan;
13. 
In accordance with Air Quality
Assessment;
14. 
In accordance with Apex Acoustic report;
15. 
Internal dwelling noise to not exceed
27dB(A);
16. 
Solar panels details;
17. 
Implementation of cycle parking;
18. 
Details of Highway Works;
19. 
Amendments to Higham Place;
20. 
Amendments to double yellow lines;
21. 
Construction Method Statement;
22. 
Demolition Methodology including
walkways;
23. 
Implementation of refuse storage;
24. 
Details of a Refuse Strategy;
25. 
No external refuse outside of the
premises;
26. 
Details of a pick-up / drop off management
plan;
27. 
Restriction of residents parking permits;
28. 
Stopping up of highway including
walkways;
29. 
Wind Mitigation details;
30. 
Confirmation of efficacy of the wind
mitigation;
31. 
Confirmation of layout and mix of uses in the
‘social amenity’ space;
32. 
Surface water drainage scheme;
33. 
Rain water harvesting;
34. 
Green roof details;
35. 
Blue roof details;
36. 
Drainage Validation – Prior to
occupation;
37. 
Lighting strategy;
38. 
CCTV strategy;
39. 
Hard and soft landscaping details;
40. 
Landscape management and maintenance
plan;
41. 
Stockholm Method details (trees);
42. 
Full detailed planting plan and management and
maintenance;
43. 
Furniture details;
44. 
Restriction of telecommunications equipment on
roof;
45. 
Details of plant screening on roof.

(iii) 
It was also agreed that in the event that a
satisfactory section 106 agreement covering the issues raised above
is not received by 1 January 2027 the application be refused for
its failure to make adequate provision in this regard contrary to
Policy DEL1 of the CSUCP unless an extension of time is agreed to
the satisfaction of the Assistant Director Planning in consultation
with the Chair and Vice Chairs of the Planning
Committee.

 

(iv) 
It was also agreed that delegated authority
be given to the Assistant Director Planning, in consultation with
the Chair and Vice Chairs of Planning Committee, to amend, add or
omit conditions and heads of terms of the section 106 legal
agreement, where appropriate, to ensure the application complies
with relevant development plan policies and national planning
guidance.

