Committee was minded to grant planning
permission for application reference 2025/1251/01/DET:
 
 
(i) 
Subject to a Section 106 agreement to
secure:

 
· 
Funding of Car club bay - £20,000;
· 
EV charging points - £20,000;
· 
TEMP - £2,500;
· 
Open Space Contribution - £92,072;
· 
BNG Monitoring £4,998;
· 
Associated costs arising from monitoring;
· 
Monitoring of SuDS maintenance -
£10,000;
· 
The provision of 5 heavy standard street trees to be
planted and maintained by the developer for the lifetime of the
development;
· 
Off site tree planting - £36,159;
· 
Overage agreement to secure future provision of off
site affordable housing up to the value of £623,832 if proven
viable.
 
(ii) 
Subject to the following conditions:
 
1. 
3 year consent;
2. 
List of approved drawings;
3. 
Details of car parking to be submitted (accessible
parking);
4. 
a Car Park management Plan;
5. 
Construction Method Statement;
6. 
No external refuse outside of the
premises;
7. 
Details of Electric Vehicle Charging
Points;

8. 
Servicing and deliveries management plan;
9. 
No local parking permits;
10. 
Implementation of the findings of the acoustic
report; 
11. 
Details of extraction in order to prevent
odour; 
12. 
Delivery hours; 
13. 
Submission of remediation scheme; 
14. 
Implementation of approved remediation
scheme; 
15. 
Reporting of unexpected
contamination; 
16. 
Further investigatory/remedial
works; 
17. 
Confirmation that the site has been made safe and
stable prior to occupation; 
18. 
Materials;
19. 
Findings of acoustic assessment are
implemented;
20. 
Operating hours for service layby;
21. 
Public Art;
22. 
Watching Brief;
23. 
Watching Brief Report;
24. 
Construction Ecological Management Plan;
25. 
Sensitive Lighting;
26. 
Bat Licence;
27. 
Bat Working Method Statement;
28. 
Bat and Bird Box Installation;
29. 
Hedgehog Hibernacula;
30. 
Hedgehog Highways;
31. 
Green Roofs;
32. 
Management of Invasive Non Native
Species;
33. 
Boundary treatments;
34. 
Surface Water Drainage Scheme;
35. 
Rainwater harvesting;
36. 
Blue roof;
37. 
Drainage validation; and
38. 
Details of access/visitor entry system.
 
(iii) 
It was also agreed that in the event
that a satisfactory section 106 agreement covering the issues
raised above is not received by 30th November 2026 that
the application be refused for its failure to make adequate
provision in this regard contrary to Policy DEL1 of the CSUCP
unless an extension of time is agreed to the satisfaction of
the Assistant Director Planning
in consultation with the Chair and Vice Chairs of
the Planning Committee.
 
(iv) 
It was also agreed that delegated authority
be given to the Assistant Director
Planning, in consultation with the Chair and
Vice Chairs of Planning Committee, to amend, add or omit conditions
and heads of terms of the section 106 legal agreement, where
appropriate, to ensure the application complies with relevant
development plan policies and national planning
guidance.

Planning permission for application reference 2024/1577/01/DET
be granted:
 
 i. 
Subject to a section 106 agreement to secure:
Overage clause to cover affordable housing and open
space
 

ii. 
Subject to the following conditions:
 

1. 
3 year
consent;

2. 
List of approved drawings;

3. 
Samples of all external building materials,
including sample panels where relevant;

4. 
Details of solar panels;

5. 
Demolition Method Statement;

6. 
Building recording;

7. 
Removal of roller shutter on the public
house;

8. 
Watching brief;

9. 
Watching brief report;

10.Archaeology - Publication Report Condition;

11.Protection of Nesting Birds;

12.Bat
Working Method Statement;

13.Bat
and Bird Box Installation;

14.Site
Characterisation;

15.Submission of Remediation Scheme;

16.Implementation of Approved Remediation Scheme;

17.Reporting of Unexpected Contamination;

18.Details of cycle parking to be submitted
(residential);

19.Implementation of cycle parking (commercial);

20.Details of Highway Works, reinstate footway on Westgate
Road;

21.Details of EV charging points;

22.Demolition and Construction Management Plan (PSR);

23.No
external refuse outside of the premises;

24.Implementation of servicing and refuse strategy;

25.Properties will not be eligible for parking permits;

26.Landscape plan showing boundary treatments, gates and hard
landscaping;

27.Details of boundary treatments;

28.Implementation of aforementioned
Public Benefits.

29.No
demolition until contract let for future build.

 

iii. 
It was also agreed that in the event that a
satisfactory section 106 agreement covering the issues raised above
is not received by 30 September 2026 the application be refused for
its failure to make adequate provision in this regard contrary to
Policy DEL1 of the CSUCP, unless an extension of time is agreed to
the satisfaction of the Assistant Director Planning in consultation
with the Chair and Vice Chairs of the Planning
Committee.
 

iv. 
It was also agreed that delegated authority
be given to the Assistant Director Planning, in consultation with
the Chair and Vice Chairs of Planning Committee, to amend, add or
omit conditions where appropriate and heads of terms of the section
106 legal agreement, to ensure the application complies with
relevant development plan policies and national planning
guidance.

Planning permission
for application reference 2025/0537/01/DET be granted:
 
 i. 
Subject to a section 106 agreement to secure:
 

­ 
Tree replacements £96,621.00;

­ 
SuDS monitoring £10,000;

­ 
Training and employment management plan £2500; and

­ 
Associated monitoring costs arising from the above planning
obligations.
 
ii. 
Subject to the following conditions:
 

1. 
3-year consent;

2. 
List of approved drawings;

3. 
Submission of remediation scheme;

4. 
Submission of construction method statement;

5. 
Erection of tree protection fencing;

6. 
Submission of hard and soft landscaping details;

7. 
Submission of method statement for hedgehogs;

8. 
Submission of details of hedgehog hibernacula;

9. 
Submission of details of proposed drainage components;

10.Submission of
details of bat and bird boxes;

11.Submission of
details of external elevational treatment;

12.Submission of
details of plant and attenuation measures;

